-- title:
--   Finiteness of S/mathfrak m_S^k over R under surjective residue map
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ and $S$ be commutative rings with $S$ Noetherian, both local, and let $S$ be an $R$-algebra whose structure morphism $\operatorname{algebraMap} R S$ is a local homomorphism (it pulls the maximal ideal of $S$ back into the maximal ideal of $R$). Assume that the induced map of residue fields $\kappa(R) \to \kappa(S)$, namely `IsLocalRing.ResidueField.map (algebraMap R S)`, is surjective. Then for every natural number $k$ the quotient ring $S/\mathfrak m_S^{\,k}$, where $\mathfrak m_S$ is the maximal ideal of $S$, is a finite (i.e. finitely generated) module over $R$ via the algebra structure. No flatness is assumed, and nothing is assumed about the ideal generated by the image of $\mathfrak m_R$ in $S$; $R$ itself need not be Noetherian.
--
--   This is the finiteness statement underlying the comparison of a local algebra with its base when the residue field extension is trivial: the truncations $S/\mathfrak m_S^k$ are finite over $R$. It is used in the construction of isomorphisms of adic completions ([`IsLocalRing.exists_adicCompletion_ringEquiv_of_flat_of_map_maximalIdeal_eq_of_residue_surjective`](thm.html#IsLocalRing.exists_adicCompletion_ringEquiv_of_flat_of_map_maximalIdeal_eq_of_residue_surjective)), in the surjectivity of $R \to S/\mathfrak m_S^k$ under the further hypothesis on $\mathfrak m_R S$, and in the study of jets for the partial action on Jacobians with good reduction.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsLocalRing_moduleFinite_quotient_maximalIdeal_pow_of_residueField_map_surjective.lean

